<title>
Front Pillar Upper Tape Removal and Installation
</title>
<attention4>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Wrinkle of the tape or trapping of foreign material like air under the tape spoils its appearance and adhesive strength.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
To avoid wrinkle or trapping of foreign material, prepare body surface where the tape is stuck degreasing and cleaning with white gasoline and carefully stick the tape.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Windshield molding edge can be damaged especially when pushing out the edge line once pushed into the bottom.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Use a small flat-bladed screwdriver wrapped with masking tape so that the edge line is not damaged.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Deteriorated windshield molding by aging could be damaged when pushing in or out the edge line.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Remove the windshield molding and install a new one if necessary. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A9506002"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention4>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Edge line of windshield molding interferes sticking the tape at the corner. Therefore, using a plastic rule or the like, push the molding edge line into the bottom of the gutter.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
After sticking the tape, inserting a small flat-bladed screwdriver wrapped with masking tape (a small flat tool without having sharp edges) under the molding, carefully push out the molding edge line as it was.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A9806014001">
<title>
Removal
</title>
<attention2>
<ptxt>
Heated body panel by hot air drier and the hot air itself could be hot enough to get burned.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Carefully work for removal of the tape on the panel.
</ptxt>
</attention2>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Recommended heating temperature for the tape is about 60 &#176;C (140 &#176;F).
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove windshield if necessary. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A9506002"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove front pillar lower molding. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A9A06004"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Using a hot air drier, heat front pillar outer upper tape (1).
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Peel off an edge of the front pillar upper tape and remove it parallel to the vehicle body.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A980012.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "67.722mm" ver = "01" gw = "214" gh = "175"/>
</figure>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
